hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15405","Waki narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Hizam, that he passed by some people of the dhimmah who had been made to stand in the sun in Sham, so he said: What are these? They said: Something of the kharaj remains due from them. So he said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will punish on the Day of Resurrection those who punish people. He said: And the commander of the people that day was Umayr ibn Sad over Filastin. He said: So he entered upon him and told him, and he let them go."
"15406","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Hisham ibn Hakim, that he passed in Sham by some Nabateans who had been made to stand in the sun, and he mentioned its meaning."
"15407","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri and Hisham ibn Urwah, that both of them narrated to him, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that Hisham ibn Hakim saw some people of the dhimmah standing in the sun, so he said: What are these? So they said: They are of the people of the jizyah. So he entered upon Umayr ibn Sad, and he was over a part of Sham, so Hisham said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever punishes people in this world, Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, will punish him. So Umayr said: Let them go."
"15408","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Safwan narrated to us, Shurayh ibn Ubayd al-Hadrami and others narrated to me, he said: Iyad ibn Ghanm flogged the chief of Dariya when it was conquered, so Hisham ibn Hakim spoke harshly to him until Iyad became angry. Then he remained for some nights, then Hisham ibn Hakim came to him and apologized to him. Then Hisham said to Iyad: Did you not hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Among the most severely punished of people are those most severe in punishing people in this world. So Iyad ibn Ghanm said: O Hisham ibn Hakim, we have heard what you heard and seen what you saw. Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever wants to advise a ruler in a matter, let him not show it to him openly, but let him take him by his hand and be alone with him. If he accepts from him, then that is it, and if not, he has discharged what was upon him toward him. And indeed you, O Hisham, are surely the bold one, since you dare against the ruler of Allah. Why did you not fear that the ruler might kill you, so you would be one killed by the ruler of Allah, the Blessed and Exalted."
"15409","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, that it reached him that Iyad ibn Ghanm saw some Nabateans being sunned for the jizyah, so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, will punish those who punish people in this world."
"15410","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Hisham ibn Hakim ibn Hizam found Iyad ibn Ghanm, while he was over Hims, sunning some Nabateans for payment of the jizyah, so Hisham said to him: What is this, O Iyad? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, will punish those who punish people in this world."
"15411","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Iyad ibn Ghanm and Hisham ibn Hakim ibn Hizam passed by the governor of Hims while he was sunning Nabateans in the sun, so one of them said to the governor: What is this, O so-and-so? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, will punish those who punish people in this world."
